# Easy Fish Tacos with Cumin Lime Slaw

Based on [https://www.budgetbytes.com/fish-tacos-with-cumin-lime-slaw/](https://www.budgetbytes.com/fish-tacos-with-cumin-lime-slaw) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251122031013/https://www.budgetbytes.com/fish-tacos-with-cumin-lime-slaw/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Cumin Lime Coleslaw

- [ ] 1/4 cup [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }
- [ ] 1 [lime]{ ing="lime" } (1 Tbsp juice)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/8 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 1/2 of a 16 oz bag [coleslaw mix]{ ing="coleslaw-mix" } (shredded cabbage and carrots)
- [ ] 2 [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, sliced

### Tacos

- [ ] 8 small [corn tortillas]{ ing="corn-tortillas" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1/8 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [cooking oil]{ ing="cooking-oil" } (divided)
- [ ] 1 lb [cod fillets]{ ing="cod-fillets" }
- [ ] 1 [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, sliced
- [ ] 1 [jalapeño]{ ing="jalapeno" }, sliced

## Recipe

1. Toast [tortillas]{ ing="corn-tortillas" } in a dry skillet over medium heat until browned on each side; stack and cover with foil.
1. Prepare the coleslaw dressing by combining [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }, [lime]{ ing="lime" } juice, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, cayenne, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }.
1. [Mix]{ ing="coleslaw-mix" } coleslaw base with [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" } and dressing; refrigerate until needed.
1. Season fish pieces with combined [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }, cumin, [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }, and salt.
1. Cook fish in batches using [oil]{ ing="cooking-oil" } until firm, opaque, and flaked easily (few minutes per side).
1. Assemble tacos with fish, [avocado]{ ing="avocado" } slices, coleslaw, and [jalapeño]{ ing="jalapeno" } on tortillas.

## Notes

- Suitable alternatives include tilapia, mahi mahi, or halibut instead of cod
